# The first lookup of a boot (`make test-net-lookup`, which turns @PORT@ into
# the test web server's port). The disk says `net.dns = 10.0.2.2`: the guest
# asks tools/test-dns on the host's 127.0.0.1, which answers `slow.zoraya`
# and `slowweb.zoraya` with 10.0.2.2 after 3 s, never answers
# `silent.zoraya` and `silentweb.zoraya`, and says NXDOMAIN for any other.
# The capture of the run is checked afterwards (zoraya-test-dns
# --check-pcap): one ARP request for the server before the first query, and
# the echo request and the SYN leave as soon as their names are answered.
! panicked
! first process ended
! did not answer
< Type help to begin, or help tour.
< \r\n~>
# The lease takes a few hundred milliseconds under TCG.
> sleep 3\r
< \r\n~>
# The first network command of the boot: `ping` by name, answered late (the
# resolver asks again at 1 s and 2 s, the first answer comes at 3 s). The
# answer is the gateway, a local address, so `+net 10.0.2.2` covers it.
> +net 10.0.2.2 ping -c 2 slow.zoraya\r
< PING slow.zoraya (10.0.2.2): 2 requests
< 2 sent, 2 received, 0% loss
< \r\n~>
# `fetch` by name, its own late lookup.
> +net 10.0.2.2 fetch --sum http://slowweb.zoraya:@PORT@/pattern/1000\r
< 1000 bytes fnv1a @SUM1K@ in
< \r\n~>
# A name no server answers: `netd` answers at its lookup bound (8 s), and
# says so; the clients waited for it.
> ping silent.zoraya\r
< the name lookup timed out
< \r\n~>
> fetch http://silentweb.zoraya/\r
< the name lookup timed out
< \r\n~>
# A name that does not exist is not a timeout.
> ping nothing.zoraya\r
< the name has no address
< \r\n~>
x power off
> poweroff\r
